  message: "Done in PR #3484 (ADR-0026). Audit went broader than the WI's named ipc_calls+ipc_event scope to cover the full IPC-shaped family (7 values across Tauri/Electron/Phoenix/WebSocket/MQ): zero CANONICAL, six FOLD (ipc_calls→calls+protocol=ipc; ipc_event/message_send/websocket_message/message_queue→event_publishes+channel_kind in {ipc,websocket,queue}; websocket_connection→references+construct=websocket_endpoint), one DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD (message_receive — same converse-direction shape problem as ADR-0025's event_subscribes). Cross-ADR overlap: message_queue and ADR-0025's enqueues fold to the same target (event_publishes+channel_kind=queue) — confirms the publish-family fold is protocol-agnostic. Registry descriptions updated; no axis reclassifications, no SCHEMA_VERSION bump (description-only). Phase 3 producer migration is WI-hahap-farid (narrow scope, may need expansion — discussed there)."  # 8517
